n how many different ways can 4 students be selected from a group of 7 students?

A) 21
B) 28
C) 35
D) 42

Answer: C) 35

Explanation:

Since we are selecting students and their order does not matter, use combinations:

$$ ^nC_r=\frac{n!}{r!(n-r)!} $$

Here:

$$ ^7C_4=\frac{7!}{4!3!} $$

Cancel \(4!\):

$$ =\frac{7\times6\times5}{3\times2\times1} $$
=
6
210
	​

=
35
	​
